    "description": "Lumber camp (sawmill), level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. A miniature sawmill (16 x 11): a short open mill shed (dark oak frame on cobblestone feet, oak roof with dark oak eaves and trim) with the saw bench in the middle, a sash-saw frame whose belt drives the blade on the carriage line; the grindstone (workstation). L1 the shed, the saw and plank stacks; L2 a waterwheel on the end and the log yard; L3 a crane over the logs, a drying rack, a sign and saplings. Not yet builder-tested: stonecutter. Decoration step adds: water.",
    "changes": "About a third smaller (16 x 11, a shorter and lower hall) and each level now adds its own big piece: L1 the shed and saw, L2 the waterwheel and log yard, L3 the crane, drying rack and sign.",
